{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"事件驱动基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cloud-infrastructure/event-driven-architecture/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"event-driven-fundamentals","title":"事件驱动基础概念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cloud-infrastructure/event-driven-architecture/foundations/event-driven-fundamentals","wordCount":1663,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"event-types-and-topology","title":"事件类型与拓扑模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cloud-infrastructure/event-driven-architecture/foundations/event-types-and-topology","wordCount":1539,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"eventual-consistency","title":"最终一致性与 CAP 权衡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cloud-infrastructure/event-driven-architecture/foundations/eventual-consistency","wordCount":1715,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"事件驱动基础\">事件驱动基础</h1><p>本章建立事件驱动架构的理论根基。从「什么是事件」这个看似简单却常被混淆的概念出发，逐步展开 EDA 的四种核心拓扑模式，并深入最终一致性的理论框架——理解为什么 EDA 天然拥抱 BASE 而非 ACID。</p>\n<p>三篇文档的递进关系：先建立事件的精确定义与分类法，再理解事件在系统中流动的拓扑结构，最后面对 EDA 最核心的设计约束——最终一致性。这个顺序对应「What → How → Why」的认知路径。</p>\n"}